course: dictionary
lesson: 9872
title: Words from the dining table
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are easy to picture because you see them every day. A tablecloth is one of them: a large piece of cloth that covers a table. The words around it give clues. «A baby can pull a tablecloth and bring hot drinks or heavy pots down onto himself.» The pulling and the falling pots show that a tablecloth sits on the table and can slide off it.
explain: Look at how the word is built: table plus cloth. Cloth is material, like the stuff a shirt is made from, so a tablecloth is cloth for a table.
explain: Other clues help too. «Lay a tablecloth» means put one on the table before a meal, and «a clean tablecloth» means one that has not been used or stained. Test your meaning: "put a cloth on the table before a meal" still makes sense, so you know you are right.
explain: Sometimes a word works in a surprising way. «The tablecloth trick» is a science experiment: you pull the cloth away very quickly and the dishes stay on the table. The dishes are slow to start moving, and this slowness is called inertia. A slow pull drags them along with it.
fact: A tablecloth is a large piece of cloth that covers a table.
fact: A tablecloth protects the table and makes it look nice, especially at meals.
fact: «Lay a tablecloth» means put one on the table before a meal.
fact: Tablecloths are used at meals, parties and picnics.
fact: Pulling hard on a hanging tablecloth can bring hot drinks or heavy things down, so keep little children away from it.
exercise: What is a tablecloth? | A small towel for drying your hands | A tall tree in a garden | *A large piece of cloth that covers a table | A soft blanket for a bed
exercise: «Put a clean tablecloth on the table before the party.» What does clean mean here? | *Not used or stained | Dirty and stained | Pulled quickly | Very wet
exercise: In «the tablecloth trick», why do the dishes stay on the table when the cloth is pulled quickly? | *They are slow to start moving | They are glued to the table | They are going to break | They are very heavy
test: Why is it dangerous for a small child to pull a hanging tablecloth? | It makes the table too clean | *It can bring hot drinks or heavy things down onto them | It tears the table | It is too soft to hold anything
test: Which phrase means the same as "lay a tablecloth"? | To fold a tablecloth into a box | To pull a tablecloth off quickly | To wash a tablecloth in the sink | *To put a tablecloth on the table
exam: What does the tablecloth trick show about how dishes move? | *Dishes are slow to start moving, so a quick pull can leave them behind | Tablecloths can fly | Dishes are always very light | Dishes always move when a cloth touches them
